  "question": {
    "text": "Five digit numbers are formed using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;with repetitions and are written in descending order with serial numbers. For example, the number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>77777</mn></math> has serial number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Then the serial number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35337</mn></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
